 result←object(State ∆Text)arg;text;tunits;punits;t
 ⍝ Rather than building a handle, the ?Text operation returns the size of the bounding box that will be required around the provided text

 ⍝ '?Text' text ...

 result←⍬
 :If 0=≢arg ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Empty command is ignored
 arg←,⊆,arg ⍝ Force to a nested vector of items
 ⍝ If arg[2] is a number, APL+Win is producing a WI LENGTH ERROR instead of a DOMAIN ERROR for some reason - I'm going to ignore that idiosyncrasy
 'DOMAIN ERROR'##.Error∨/~##.IsChar¨arg
 (tunits punits)←2↑##.Classes._supp.MyUnits State

 :For text :In arg
     text←'?Text'##.ToChar text ⍝ Convert any numerics into plain characters
     t←,~text∊⎕UCS 13 ⋄ (t/,text)←object ##.QuadAV t/,text ⍝ Convert to APL font codepoints if needed
     result,←⊂(punits÷tunits)×object ##.Classes._supp.GetTextSize text(⎕VGET State.FontObj)1
 :EndFor

⍝? Does this need to require a default State.FontObj? How would we work without it?
